{%- comment -%}
  Suppressed on templates that already carry their own pair.

  This section now renders from the footer group, i.e. on every page. About has
  its own bespoke CTA pair ("Come and see it" / "Or start with a glass") and
  the generic closers landed directly beneath it — two pairs of the same shape,
  stacked, doing the same job.

  Matched on template suffix and name, so "our-story" covers /pages/about-us
  whatever the page handle becomes. Comma separated, editable, and empty by
  default so the section behaves normally anywhere else it is used.

  max_blocks is 3 while the band still RENDERS two — the loop below stops at
  two survivors. The third card exists so a page that suppresses one of them
  still has a pair to draw from. Leaving it at 2 made Shopify reject the whole
  footer group; the GitHub sync said nothing and only themeFilesUpsert named
  the reason. Notes like this belong here and not in the schema JSON: an
  unrecognised key in there is itself one of the silent rejection modes.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign hide_list = section.settings.hide_on_templates | default: '' | downcase | split: ',' -%}
{%- assign this_template = template.suffix | default: template.name | downcase -%}
{%- assign skip_here = false -%}
{%- comment -%}
  `candidate`, NOT `assign t = t | strip`. Inside a for loop the iteration
  variable wins on read, so assigning back to `t` looked like it stripped the
  value and silently did nothing. "our-story" matched because it is first in
  the list and carries no leading space; " stockists" never matched, and the
  stockists page rendered two pairs of closing cards for it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- for t in hide_list -%}
  {%- assign candidate = t | strip -%}
  {%- if candidate != blank and candidate == this_template -%}{%- assign skip_here = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- if skip_here -%}
  {%- comment -%} nothing rendered here by design {%- endcomment -%}
{%- else -%}
{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
<div class="non-split"{% if section.settings.max_height > 0 %} style="--non-split-max: {{ section.settings.max_height }}px"{% endif %}>
  {%- comment -%}
    The band is always a PAIR. There are three cards defined and at most one of
    them suppresses itself on any given page, so taking the first two survivors
    gives two everywhere: the shop page loses "Skip the questions?" and gains
    NONHQ, the NONHQ page loses NONHQ and keeps the range. Before this the shop
    page closed with a single card stretched across the full width.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign rendered = 0 -%}
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- if rendered >= 2 -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Do not offer someone a door into the room they are standing in.

      The closers are one global pair rendered under every page, which is why
      the stockists page was closing with "Find a stockist" and the shop page
      with "Shop the range". A card whose link resolves to the current page is
      skipped rather than rendered dead.

      `contains` rather than `==` because request.path carries the market and
      locale prefix — /en-au/pages/store-locator against a /pages/store-locator
      setting — so an equality test would never fire outside the primary
      market. A bare "/" is excluded: it is inside every path.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign target = block.settings.link | split: '?' | first -%}
    {%- assign is_here = false -%}
    {%- if target != blank and target != '/' and request.path contains target -%}
      {%- assign is_here = true -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- unless is_here -%}
    {%- assign rendered = rendered | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- assign alt_text = block.settings.image_alt | default: block.settings.title -%}
    <div class="non-split__cell" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
      {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
        {{
          block.settings.image
          | image_url: width: 1200, format: 'webp'
          | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '600,900,1200', class: 'non-split__img', alt: alt_text
        }}
      {%- elsif block.settings.image_url != blank -%}
        {% render 'cdn-image',
           url: block.settings.image_url,
           alt: alt_text,
           class: 'non-split__img',
           sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 50vw, 100vw' %}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A visible placeholder rather than nothing. An empty panel reads as a
          layout bug; a placeholder reads as "an image belongs here", which is
          what it is.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {{ 'lifestyle-2' | placeholder_svg_tag }}
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="non-split__body">
        <div class="non-split__title">{{ block.settings.title }}</div>
        <p class="non-split__text">{{ block.settings.text }}</p>
        {%- if block.settings.link_label != blank -%}
          <a class="non-split__link" href="{{ block.settings.link }}">{{ block.settings.link_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- endunless -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
</div>

{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Split feature",
  "max_blocks": 3,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hide_on_templates",
      "label": "Hide on templates",
      "info": "Comma-separated template suffixes, e.g. our-story. Use when a page already has its own pair of these."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "max_height",
      "label": "Maximum image height",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 900,
      "step": 20,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "Caps how tall the pictures may grow on a wide screen. 0 leaves them sized by the shape above."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "bg_color",
      "label": "Background"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Text colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "font_family",
      "label": "Font",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "",
          "label": "Theme default"
        },
        {
          "value": "sans",
          "label": "Helvetica (all text)"
        },
        {
          "value": "mono",
          "label": "JetBrains Mono (all text)"
        }
      ],
      "default": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "text_scale",
      "label": "Text size",
      "min": 70,
      "max": 150,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "info": "Scales every text size in this section together."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "section_padding",
      "label": "Vertical padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 8,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "0 keeps the section's own spacing."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "cell",
      "name": "Panel",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Image",
          "info": "Overrides the image URL below."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "image_url",
          "label": "Image URL",
          "info": "Used when no image is picked. Points at an image already on the store's CDN."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "image_alt",
          "label": "Image alt text",
          "info": "Describes the photo for screen readers. Falls back to the title."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "link_label",
          "label": "Link label"
        },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "link",
          "label": "Link"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Split feature"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}

